\", rmErr)\n469\t\t}\n470\t\n471\t\t// Amend HEAD so attach treats this as an existing-checkpoint case.\n472\t\trunGitInDir(t, repoRoot, \"commit\", \"--amend\", \"-m\", \"init\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: \"+alicesCheckpoint.String())\n473\t\n474\t\tsessionID := \"bob-attempted-attach\"\n475\t\tsetupClaudeTranscript(t, sessionID, `{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hi\"},\"uuid\":\"u1\"}\n476\t`)\n477\t\n478\t\tvar out bytes.Buffer\n479\t\terr = runAttach(context.Background(), &out, sessionID, agent.AgentNameClaudeCode, true)\n480\t\tif err == nil {\n481\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected attach to refuse when checkpoint is only in the remote-tracking ref\")\n482\t\t}\n483\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"missing from the local entire/checkpoints/v1 branch\") {\n484\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"error should explain the local-branch gap; got: %v\", err)\n485\t\t}\n486\t\n487\t\t// Local branch must still not exist — attach should not have created a\n488\t\t// fresh orphan on refuse.\n489\t\tif _, refErr := repo.Reference(localRef, true); refErr == nil {\n490\t\t\tt.Error(\"local entire/checkpoints/v1 branch was created despite refuse; would clobber remote on push\")\n491\t\t}\n492\t\n493\t\t// Remote-tracking ref must still hold Alice's untouched data.\n494\t\tremoteRef, err := repo.Reference(remoteTrackingRef, true)\n495\t\tif err != nil {\n496\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"remote-tracking ref missing: %v\", err)\n497\t\t}\n498\t\tif remoteRef.Hash() != populated.Hash() {\n499\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"remote-tracking ref moved from %s to %s\", populated.Hash(), remoteRef.Hash())\n500\t\t}\n501\t}\n502\t\n503\t// In v2-only mode, the refuse hint must reference the v2 /main ref and\n504\t// its fully-qualified refspec (refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main lives under\n505\t// refs/entire/, not refs/heads/, so a short refspec won't resolve).\n506\tfunc TestAttach_RefuseHint_V2Only(t *testing.T) {\n507\t\tsetupAttachTestRepo(t)\n508\t\n509\t\trepoRoot := mustGetwd(t)\n510\t\tsetAttachCheckpointsV2Only(t, repoRoot)\n511\t\n512\t\trunGitInDir(t, repoRoot, \"commit\", \"--amend\", \"-m\", \"init\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: ffffffffeeee\")\n513\t\n514\t\tsessionID := \"v2-orphaned-attach\"\n515\t\tsetupClaudeTranscript(t, sessionID, `{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hi\"},\"uuid\":\"u1\"}\n516\t`)\n517\t\n518\t\tvar out bytes.Buffer\n519\t\terr := runAttach(context.Background(), &out, sessionID, agent.AgentNameClaudeCode, true)\n520\t\tif err == nil {\n521\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected v2-only attach to refuse when checkpoint is missing\")\n522\t\t}\n523\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"missing from the local v2 /main ref\") {\n524\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"error should describe the v2 /main ref; got: %v\", err)\n525\t\t}\n526\t\tv2Refspec := paths.V2MainRefName + \":\" + paths.V2MainRefName\n527\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), v2Refspec) {\n528\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"error should include v2 refspec %q; got: %v\", v2Refspec, err)\n529\t\t}\n530\t\t// And must NOT suggest the v1 refspec.\n531\t\tif strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"entire/checkpoints/v1:entire/checkpoints/v1\") {\n532\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"v2-only hint should not reference the v1 branch; got: %v\", err)\n533\t\t}\n534\t}\n535\t\n536\tfunc TestAttach_PopulatesTokenUsage(t *testing.T) {\n537\t\tsetupAttachTestRepo(t)\n538\t\n539\t\tsessionID := \"test-attach-token-usage\"\n540\t\tsetupClaudeTranscript(t, sessionID, `{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hello\"},\"uuid\":\"u1\"}\n541\t{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_1\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"hi\"}],\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0}},\"uuid\":\"a1\"}\n542\t`)\n543\t\n544\t\tvar out bytes.Buffer\n545\t\tif err := runAttach(context.Background(), &out, sessionID, agent.AgentNameClaudeCode, true); err != nil {\n546\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"runAttach failed: %v\", err)\n547\t\t}\n54